     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled daily dose of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. The usual maximum single dose is 850 mg to 1,000 mg. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is substantially higher, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for IR)\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intended, tell me and I'll reconsider. I'd suggest adding a note on the order explaining the rationale. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
