     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it, but 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of metformin. I don't know of any clinical situation where that dose is appropriate, and it could seriously harm the patient through lactic acidosis. A resident-level confirmation alone isn't enough for me to enter it.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals right now, or any other dose up to 2,550 mg/day.\n- **Discuss it with your attending or a clinical pharmacist.** If there's a reason for an exceptional dose, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, they can help. The order would also need a documented rationale.\n- **Check the source.** If the 1,700 mg came from a note or handoff, it may be a total daily dose that was mistaken for a per-dose amount.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
